WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have three boys.
-Yes.

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:04.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were saying backstage --
11, 9, and 7. Right?

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do they like that their dad's
in a rock band?

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:07.574 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Do they go to shows?

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-They're into it.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.776 line:92%
They're so used to it, you know.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
Since they were born,
that's what I do.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:16.416
And they -- you know, they love
music and they've been to gigs.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:19.819
But none of them have ever made
it through an entire gig

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.221 size:84% position:42% line:92%
without falling asleep.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, really?

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because we go on at 9:00.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so --
I mean, that's already,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, that's bedtime.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:27.927 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So my wife's documented
a couple instances

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
on her Instagram where they're
just like dozing off.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:36.369
And I'm, like, on fire on stage,
like, giving it.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.704 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And it's pretty funny.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.106 line:92%
-You did the Panorama festival.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:40.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here in New York.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:46.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you -- you brought someone
from the audience

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.581 line:92%
up on stage to play drums.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.049 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How does that happen?
What happens?

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-They bring signs.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, so someone was
holding a sign saying --

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:54.954 line:92%
-Yeah, we had never done it --

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
until November last year,
this hadn't happened.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.192 line:92%
A kid in Dublin brought a sign.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wanted to play keyboards
on a song of ours

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.496 line:92%
called "A Dustland Fairytale."

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:06.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we brought him up
and it was -- it was amazing.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:09.969
Because people are already,
you know, coming together

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
at this concert and they all
agree on something

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's beautiful
to have that sort of

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.410 line:92%
congregation of people cheering.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.948
But when that kid came on stage,
everybody was rooting for him.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were rooting for him.
And it was beautiful.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.253
Then all of a sudden, it just
took on a whole life of its own.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now at every gig,
there are people with signs.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:30.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So you had a --

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.960
Let's take a look at the drummer
you brought up here in New York.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.262 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.898 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.409 size:75% position:38%
-He's singing along.
-That's fantastic!

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.477 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:53.947 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So, how -- be honest.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
How often is it good?
-Okay.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.353 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:04.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is -- I think 60 --
63% of the time.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a good --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:06.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.228
-And I will say this is a photo,
you know, obviously taken.

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here you are getting --
I mean, look at that crowd.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at the amount of people
you got to perform with.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's really incredible
that you do that.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do want to say, I know
I told you this once before.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met in 2008
when you did "SNL"

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:18.972 line:92%
and my mom was at the show,

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I introduced you to my mom
and you were so polite.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is sort of
a famous story

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
because a lot of people
overheard her.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you went back
to your dressing room

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.946
and we were walking down
the hall and my mom said,

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.681
"I don't know why they call them
The Killers.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:31.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
They couldn't be nicer."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's as true today
as it was then.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.288
Thanks so much for being here,
man. I really appreciate it.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.357 line:92%
Brandon Flowers, everybody!

